<title>USA: Stage Stores proceeds with IPO, sees better market.</title>
<headline>Stage Stores proceeds with IPO, sees better market.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stage Stores Inc, the parent company of Specialty Retailers Inc, said on Tuesday that it will proceed with its initial public offering, citing improved conditions in the IPO market.</p>
<p>Lead underwriter CS First Boston said the offering of 10 million shares is expected to price between $14 and $16 a share.</p>
<p>The company has applied to trade on the Nasdaq National Market under the symbol &quot;STGE&quot; and the offering is expected to go public the week of October 21, the underwriter said.</p>
</text>
